== Notes
1. The disk filled during the first run. At 14:27Z the instance's root volume was 100% full with 7 MiB free. The
   first chain was still in `make core-test`, which writes about 3,600 coverage .dat files of 5-11 MB each. That
   core-test stopped (rc=2), and riscv-tests and the sim targets then failed at once (rc=1, 1 s).
   - The first full ACT run lost 77 result rows: 2500/2501 PASS with a row-count mismatch.
   - Three Linux stress runs (ptw2_lat45, exec_lat45, exec_lat1) lost console lines.
   Recovery:
   - My coverage files were deleted. core-test, riscv-tests and the sim targets reran in the same clean clone (chain
     A2). A janitor deleted the `nocov_*.dat` files two minutes after they were written: those are the SRAM-macro
     runs' files (COV_PREFIX=nocov), which the coverage step never reads. The `cov_*.dat` files were kept.
   - Full ACT reran in full.
   - The three stress runs restarted from scratch.
   - From 14:39Z the root volume had about 290 GB free.
   Steps that finished before 14:27Z are unaffected: lint, make test, the Linux boot, oops-ptw-*, the before side,
   and ptw2_lat1. The results above are from the clean runs.
2. ACT ELFs: the 2578-ELF sigil-core generation used by the earlier full-ACT gates
   (vivado_rnd:~/sigil-gates/third_party/riscv-arch-test/work/sigil-core/elfs, riscv-arch-test 6af53584). It was copied
   unchanged; the fingerprint (sha256 of the sorted per-ELF sha256 list) is 839ba8be...ae7f on both hosts. The ELFs are
   self-checking and DUT-independent. Here they ran on core_tb built from the gate SHA. See act_summary.txt.
3. Before side: a worktree at 5458d16 with the gate tree's simulation-only checkers (sim/Makefile.oops,
   tb/sv/sigil_oops_chk.sv, tb/sv/sigil_ptw_inv.sv, tb/cpp/oops_chk_dpi.cpp) copied in untracked. It ran the same test
   binaries. The RTL diff between base and gate is only rtl/core/sigil_core.sv and rtl/core/sigil_mmu.sv.
4. Linux simulation does not exercise the race. On the fixed RTL, both ptwstress runs end with PTWCOV pre=0: no fetch
   walk was preempted at all (the base RTL's hunter checker build has no PTWCOV). The hunters' unpatched runs of the same
   images end with stale-walk-rsp 0 at exactly the same cycle counts as the fixed RTL (ptwstress 308,934,879 and
   689,559,153; boot 261,247,447). The race is exercised by the directed tests (before_after.log), and it showed up on
   the F2.

